{"name":"Shabby Chic Pink","hex":"#efddd6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shabby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of clothing, a place, etc.: unkempt and worn or otherwise in poor condition due to age or neglect; scruffy.","Of a person: wearing ragged or very worn, and often dirty, clothing."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (something) shabby (adjective sense 1); to shabbify.","To become shabby; to shabbify."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shabby"},{"term":"chic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Elegant, stylish."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Good form; style.","A person with (a particular type of) chic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chic"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ylvis","blocks":[{"text":"Ylvis are a Norwegian comedy duo consisting of brothers Vegard and Bård Ylvisåker. They debuted as professional variety artists in 2000 and have appeared in several countries in variety shows, comedy concerts, television shows, radio shows and music videos. They hosted the Norwegian talk show I kveld med Ylvis (2011–2016). Their song and music video \"The Fox \", written and filmed for the talk show, went viral on YouTube in September 2013. The video has over 1.2 billion views as of July 2026. They released an album called Ylvis: Volume I, a compilation of ten older singles. In 2018, the brothers released a series titled Stories from Norway, in which they collected headlining stories from Norway and presented them as short musical documentaries to address satire, fun and comedy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/I_kveld_med_Ylvis.jpg/330px-I_kveld_med_Ylvis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ylvis"},{"title":"Shabby chic","blocks":[{"text":"Shabby chic is a style of interior design that chooses either furniture and furnishings for their appearance of age and signs of wear and tear or distresses new ones to achieve the same result. Unlike much genuine period décor, this style features a soft, pastel-colored, cottage look."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shabby_chic"},{"title":"Big Brother (British TV series) series 11","blocks":[{"text":"Big Brother 2010, also known as Big Brother 11, is the eleventh series of the British reality television series Big Brother, and the final series of the show to be broadcast by Channel 4. The show followed twenty-one contestants, known as housemates, who were isolated from the outside world for an extended period of time in a custom-built House. Each week, one or more of the housemates were evicted by a public vote. The last remaining housemate, Josie Gibson, was declared the winner, winning a cash prize of £100,000 and a place as a Housemate on Ultimate Big Brother, an all-star edition of Big Brother which began immediately after the conclusion of Big Brother 2010"}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/81/BB11-eye-possible-620x465.jpg/330px-BB11-eye-possible-620x465.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Brother_(British_TV_series)_series_11"},{"title":"Chic","blocks":[{"text":"Chic, meaning \"stylish\" or \"smart\", is an element of fashion. It was originally a French word."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chic"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Ylvis_-_2026-4.jpg/500px-Ylvis_-_2026-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Ylvis_-_2026-4.jpg/1280px-Ylvis_-_2026-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Ylvis_-_2026-4.jpg/500px-Ylvis_-_2026-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Performing at the Ravnedalen Live open air festival in Kristiansand, Norway, 2026","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYlvis_-_2026-4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Ylvis_-_2026-2.jpg/500px-Ylvis_-_2026-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Ylvis_-_2026-2.jpg/1280px-Ylvis_-_2026-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Ylvis_-_2026-2.jpg/500px-Ylvis_-_2026-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Performing with their younger brother Bjarte (center) at the Ravnedalen Live festival, 2026","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYlvis_-_2026-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Distressed_finish_vintage_dresser.jpg/330px-Distressed_finish_vintage_dresser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Distressed_finish_vintage_dresser.jpg/330px-Distressed_finish_vintage_dresser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A dresser with a distressed finish and mismatched drawer knobs, in Shabby chic style","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADistressed_finish_vintage_dresser.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Josie_Gibson_at_BAFTAs_2026_01.jpg/500px-Josie_Gibson_at_BAFTAs_2026_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=p